  "aiContextParagraph": "Joe Wallach, a prominent American-born businessman and television executive, died in Los Angeles at the age of 103 on the night of Friday, November 20, 2026. Wallach was known for his significant contributions to the Brazilian media landscape, having relocated to Brazil in 1965. He is recognized as one of the key founding figures behind the establishment of TV Globo, which became a dominant leader in open television viewership, as well as the cable network Globosat. His long career in the industry was marked by his role in building these major Brazilian communication institutions. His death marks the passing of a significant individual in the country's broadcast history, leaving behind a legacy that shaped the development of television programming and media operations within Brazil for several decades.",
